 | JSON Schema | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
 | Regex | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
 | Grammar | ❌ | ✅ | ✅ |
+
+### Limiting XGrammar generation batches
+
+Each XGrammar processor factory accepts `max_batch_size`. `None` leaves the
+batch unlimited; a non-negative integer sets the maximum, and zero rejects any
+nonempty generation. An unbatched sequence counts as one. The limit is checked
+when a generation starts, including after `reset()`. A rejected first call does
+not initialize generation state, so the processor can still accept a later
+valid call.
